- REST DURATION: a full night's rest is 8 hours. The character recovers 1 HP per character level
  (or 2 per level with long-term care via Heal DC 15). Ability damage heals at 1 point per night
  of rest.
- SPELL PREPARATION: arcane casters need 8 hours of rest then 1 hour of preparation to regain
  spell slots. Spontaneous casters need 8 hours of rest. Interrupted rest of fewer than 1 hour
  does not prevent recovery; more than 1 hour of interruption requires restarting.
- WATCH ORDER: if multiple characters are present, watches of equal length split the night.
  A character on watch is not resting. 8 hours of rest = 8 hours minus time on watch, so a
  2-person party needs at least 10 hours to both fully rest.
- RANDOM ENCOUNTERS: the DM should consider a random encounter check for each watch period.
  Include this as a consequence if the narrative context suggests danger.
- FATIGUE / EXHAUSTION: a fatigued character who becomes fatigued again is exhausted. 8 hours
  of rest removes fatigue. Exhaustion downgrades to fatigue after 8 hours of rest.
